    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d47">

                <pb facs="0148" n="74" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg74"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/4834</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Russian Minister of Foreign Affairs</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Tereshchenko</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the
                        Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-05-21">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 21, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received May 22, midnight.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>In taking over the direction of the Ministry of Foreign Affairs, I hasten to say
                    to you how highly the whole Russian democracy is <pb facs="0149" n="75"
                        xml:id="pg75"/> inspired with the sentiment of full solidarity with the
                    great Republic which true to its traditions of liberty has espoused the cause of
                    the coalition for the defense of justice and right. Like the United States,
                    emancipated Russia is not seeking conquest or any covetous end in the present
                    contest. The war is carried on to secure the freedom of nations and achieve
                    universal lasting peace effectively guaranteed against all later attack. I am
                    glad to find that those lofty principles which were so eloquently formulated in
                    America are striking a warm unanimous echo in free Russia now mistress of her
                    destinies.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tereshchenko</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
